# Rust
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Claude Code's PROJECT-level config. Nothing reads the copy in this repo —
# `install/setup-hooks.py` writes to ~/.claude/settings.json, in your home.
# The tracked file here was an empty `{}`, and leaving it would have made this
# directory the next place local settings (permissions, hooks) accumulate and
# ship to everyone who clones. The plugin manifest is separate and IS part of
# the product: .claude-plugin/marketplace.json stays tracked.
/.claude/

# Swift / the menu bar panel
/panel/.build/
/panel/*.app/

# Local dev-tool caches. Each of these tools also drops a .gitignore inside its
# own directory, which is not enough to rely on: Entrography's says `*` with no
# `!.gitignore` exception, so it ignores ITSELF and never reaches the repo — it
# protects only a machine that has already run the tool. That gap is not
# hypothetical. `.entrography/index.db` (4.8 MB) was committed seven times
# before anyone noticed, the first time a full day before the tool started
# writing its own ignore file at all.
#
# Listing them here instead means the rule is versioned: it holds for a fresh
# clone, for a collaborator, and for CI — none of which have run the tool.
/.entrography/
/.codegraph/

# Playwright MCP debugging artifacts: browser console logs and accessibility-
# tree snapshots. These are session-local output from driving a browser with
# the playwright MCP server; they name localhost URLs and DOM structure, not
# project content, but they are junk and the directory arrived exactly the way
# .entrography did — as a tool output nobody excluded before its first `git add`.
/.playwright-mcp/

# Editor / IDE local state. None of these are project content; they are a
# contributor's local layout and the next contributor's will differ. Listed
# here rather than left to each editor's own ignore file for the same reason
# the tool caches are: the rule has to hold on a fresh clone.
/.vscode/
/.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.#*

# OS junk that shows up on shared filesystems.
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db

# Backstop. No database or WAL sidecar belongs in this repo from anywhere in
# the tree; the entries above are only the tools we know about today, and the
# next one will arrive the same way — as an untracked directory nobody looks
# inside before `git add -A`.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
